    "text": "Elaine, also known as Elayne, Elain, or Elane, is an Arthurian heroine. the Lady of Shalott (Elaine of Astolat) wove tapestries that showed the outer world. She spied the knight Lancelot and fell in love. Knowing it would kill her, she sailed toward Camelot and died on the way. Thomas Malory's Morte D'Arthur made the tale famous from older Celtic legend. The original may have been a siren of Scotland's Clyde, at Dumbarton, who read a magic mirror. Another Elaine bore Lancelot's son Galahad. Yet another, Elaine of Garlot, was Arthur's half-sister who wed his enemy Nentres.",
